<description>
Erase each target-color object crossed by the ray pointed by the bar-and-control marker.

Input structure:
- The background is the dominant color.
- There is one three-pixel straight marker bar and one singleton control pixel adjacent to the bar center.
- The remaining non-background color forms multiple 4-connected target objects.

Rule:
- Cast a straight ray from the marker bar center in the direction away from the adjacent control pixel.
- Find every 4-connected target-color object that intersects that ray.
- Recolor all pixels of those hit target objects to the background; all other pixels stay unchanged.

Key insight:
- The whole object is erased when the center ray touches any of its pixels; the full marker bar width is not swept.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "three-pixel marker bar with an adjacent singleton control pixel",
  "path": "straight center ray from the bar center going away from the control pixel to the grid edge",
  "trajectory": "ray itself is not painted; it selects each 4-connected target-color object it crosses",
  "transform": "recolor all pixels of selected target objects to background; leave the marker and other target objects unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 9-14 rows x 10-13 cols
  colors: bg=7, target=4, bar=5, control=9 [observed]
  marker:
    bar: 3 contiguous pixels of bar_color, horizontal or vertical, not touching grid edge
    control: 1 pixel of control_color, 4-adjacent to bar center, perpendicular to bar axis
    ray_direction: from bar center away from control (along bar's perpendicular axis)
  target_objects:
    color: target_color, 4-connected components
    count: 10-18 total
    sizes: mostly 1-pixel singletons, a few 2-7 pixel clusters; median ~1
    density: 17-21% of grid cells are target_color
    hit_by_ray: exactly 2 objects intersect the center ray [observed]
    not_hit: 8-16 objects remain untouched
    placement: scattered across the grid; some pairs may be 8-adjacent; some may be adjacent to marker
  ray:
    length: 6-8 cells (bar center to grid edge, exclusive of center)
    only target_color pixels appear on the ray (no bar/control pixels)
  transform: erase (set to bg) every target object whose any pixel lies on the ray; keep all else

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size (9-14 x 10-13), bar axis (H/V), and ray direction (one of 4 cardinal dirs consistent with axis)
    2. Place bar center so ray length is 6-8 and bar does not touch grid edge; place bar (3 cells) and control (1 cell)
    3. Scatter 8-16 target objects (sizes 1-5, mostly singletons) across the grid avoiding bar/control cells; ensure none intersect the ray -- this is the OUTPUT
    4. Pick 2 of those objects to be "hit" objects; move/grow them so at least 1 pixel lands on the ray; these become the additional target objects in the INPUT
    5. Actually simpler: build output with non-hit objects only, then place 2 extra target objects (size 1-7) that each cross the ray -- this gives the input; output is input minus those 2 objects
    6. Verify: exactly 3 non-bg colors, exactly 1 bar, 1 control, >=10 total target objects, 2 hit by ray
```
